From: evilcomputer12 <martinrobotika@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 01:34:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] xodus-service: Handle UserInfoRequest.

Answer the runtime's UserInfoRequest (7) with a UserInfoResponse (8) that
says who is signed in: the identity claims of an XSTS token for the default
relying party http://xboxlive.com, title-bound (shared session, cached per
title and relying party) when the request carries ClientId + TitleId, else
from a user-only token. No stored user token means SignedIn false rather
than an error, so the game silently keeps its offline user; a token without
an xuid claim is E_FAIL, Xbox Live refusals keep the TokenAndSignature
HRESULT mapping.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
